  "body_mappings": [
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        518.4614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "Deep in a Thai rainforest, a carpenter ant breaks from its colony's column in the lofty canopy. Swaying on unsteady legs, it wanders downward, as if intoxicated, into leafy undergrowth. Around midday it clenches its jaws on a major vein underneath a leaf, about 25 centimetres above the ground."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        430.7614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.9614173228347
      ],
      "text": "By dusk the insect is lifeless, yet the bite holds rigidly. A fungus has destroyed its jaw muscles, so they cannot loosen. Two or three days later a fungal stalk pushes from its head and releases infectious spores on to the ground below, where foraging ants tread."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        323.2614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        422.2614173228347
      ],
      "text": "The invader, Ophiocordyceps unilateralis, is fussy about location. David Hughes and colleagues found the bites mostly on the north-west side of plants, where the air is humid and the temperature suits the fungus. When researchers moved infected ants higher, the fungus grew abnormally. Placed on the ground, the bodies disappeared."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        235.5614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        314.7614173228347
      ],
      "text": "In 2017 a Penn State team examined infected ants with three-dimensional microscope imaging. Fungal cells had formed an intertwined lattice around muscle fibres in the legs and jaw, a picture that evokes the strings of a puppet. Yet the fungus had not infiltrated the brain."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        147.8614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        227.0614173228347
      ],
      "text": "A Planet Earth episode, with David Attenborough's narration, showed one such ant. It helped inspire The Last of Us, a 2013 video game whose makers envisioned the parasite jumping to humans. The hypothetical scenario gave gamers a fictional nightmare."
    },
    {
      "section": "en",
      "page": 2,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        79.9614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        139.3614173228347
      ],
      "text": "The real parasite's roots run far deeper, into the geological record. A 48-million-year-old fossil leaf from Messel, in Germany, bears the same characteristic bite scars."
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        517.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        597.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "在泰国雨林深处，一只木匠蚁脱离了它的蚁群队列，在高耸的树冠上（前行）。摇摇晃晃，腿脚不稳，它向下游荡，好像喝醉了一样，进入枝叶茂密的林下植被。正午前后，它将双颚紧咬在一片叶子下方的一条主叶脉上，离地面约25厘米。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        449.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        509.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "到黄昏时，这只昆虫已无生命，那一口却仍牢牢地咬着。一种真菌摧毁了它的颚部肌肉，因此它们无法松开。两三天后，一根真菌菌柄从它头部顶出，将具有传染性的孢子释放到下方的地面上，那里有觅食的蚂蚁行走。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        380.6614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        440.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "这个入侵者，也就是偏侧蛇虫草菌，对位置很挑剔。戴维·休斯和同事发现，这些咬合点大多在植物的西北侧，那里空气潮湿，且温度适宜真菌。研究人员把受感染的蚂蚁移到更高处时，真菌长得很反常。放在地面上，尸体则不见了。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        312.1614173228347,
        461.8976377952756,
        372.1614173228347
      ],
      "text": "2017年，宾夕法尼亚州立大学的一个团队检查了受感染的蚂蚁，用的是三维显微镜成像。真菌细胞形成了相互交织的网格，围在腿部和颚部的肌肉纤维周围，一幅使人想起木偶的提线的画面。不过，真菌尚未渗入大脑。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        243.66141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        303.6614173228347
      ],
      "text": "《地球脉动》的一集，伴随着戴维·阿滕伯勒的解说，就展示了这样一只蚂蚁。它帮助启发了2013年的电子游戏《最后生还者》，游戏的制作者们设想这种寄生菌跳到了人类身上。这个假想的情景给玩家带来了一场虚构的噩梦。"
    },
    {
      "section": "zh",
      "page": 3,
      "bbox": [
        37.0,
        195.16141732283472,
        461.8976377952756,
        235.16141732283472
      ],
      "text": "现实中的寄生菌，其根源要深得多，一直延伸到地质记录之中。一片4800万年前的叶子化石，出土于德国梅塞尔，上面带有同样典型的咬合疤痕。"
    }
  ],
